## Local dev stack

Two services run in `docker-compose.yml` — Postgres (always-on) and MinIO
(opt-in via `--profile full`, needed only once `@cap.File` enters the app).

```bash
cp .env.example .env                              # first-time only
docker compose up -d postgres                     # database
bash scripts/bootstrap-storage.sh                 # MinIO + bucket (when uploads land)
```

`bootstrap-storage.sh` brings up the `minio` service, waits for it to be
ready, creates the bucket named in `S3_BUCKET_DEFAULT`, and grants
download-only anonymous read for signed-URL serving. Idempotent.

### `S3_*` env vars are the contract

`@plugin/object-store` reads **`S3_*`** vars (`S3_ENDPOINT`, `S3_REGION`,
`S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE`,
`S3_BUCKET_DEFAULT`). With those missing, the AWS SDK falls through to the
default credential chain → EC2 IMDS → `dial tcp 169.254.169.254:80`
timeout. If you see "no EC2 IMDS role found" locally, `.env` is the
problem, not the network — copy `.env.example` and restart the API.

### MinIO `_FILE` gotcha

`minio/minio:latest` defaults `MINIO_ROOT_USER_FILE` and
`MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD_FILE` to Docker-secret paths under `/run/secrets/`.
If those files don't exist (they don't, in dev), MinIO ignores
`MINIO_ROOT_USER`/`MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD` and boots with unknown root
credentials — every `mc admin` call returns `Access Denied`. The
scaffolded `docker-compose.yml` explicitly sets those `_FILE` vars to
empty strings; don't remove them.

