## Authoring idioms

Lazuli rewards a declarative style. Before hand-rolling, reach for the idiom.
The full canon — each idiom with a before/after pilot excerpt and the doctor
rule that enforces it — lives in `docs/lazuli_way.md` (upstream framework docs).
The seed `note` feature in this scaffold (`app/features/note/`) is a worked
example.

- Reach for `conventions [crud]`, not a hand-rolled create/update/delete command per resource.
- Reach for a `crud` overlay for PRODUCTION CRUD — pair `conventions [crud]` with a `crud` block (`create`/`update`/`delete` sub-blocks) carrying `policy @policy.*` / `validate @validator.*` / `input excludes <fields>` / `assign <field> = <expr>` / `emits <event>`, instead of hand-rolling the whole command just to add a policy, a default value, a field-rename, or an event. The synth merges the overlay into the generated command before lowering, so the IR is byte-identical to the hand-rolled form (no new lowering). Bare `[crud]` is only for policy-trivial, event-free resources. See `docs/lazuli_way/crud-by-convention.md`.
- Reach for `soft_delete by`, not a hand-rolled `deleted_at: DateTime optional` + `deleted_by: ID optional` pair (+ a `deleted_at = ctx.now` / `deleted_by = ctx.actor.id` delete body). The trait projects both columns (`deleted_at` + a `deleted_by` actor column populated from `ctx.actor`) and makes the `conventions [crud]` delete soft-delete-aware; bare `soft_delete` stays `deleted_at`-only. Hand-rolling the pair trips `VOCAB-SOFT-DELETE-ACTOR-001` (see `docs/lazuli_way/soft-delete.md`).
- Reach for `access: <policy>` on a field whose read == write, not a duplicated `read:`/`write:` pair spelling the same allow-list twice under `policies fields <Resource>`. `access: P` desugars to `read: P` + `write: P` (byte-identical IR + Go) and makes the symmetry intent explicit; keep explicit `read:`/`write:` only for the asymmetric minority (read and write genuinely differ). One form per field — mixing `access:` with `read:`/`write:` on the same field is a parse error. The `access:` shorthand satisfies the `field-security-policy` contract on `@pii.*`/`@cap.*` fields (see `docs/lazuli_way/field-policy.md`).
- Reach for a `defaults` block, not the same `tenancy` / `rate_limit` / `audit default` repeated on every command. Declare the shared `rate_limit "<spec>"` / `audit default` once in `defaults`; each command inherits it (a per-command value wins, `audit none` opts out). Repeating an identical `rate_limit`/`audit` on ≥3 commands draws `defaults_hoist_rate_limit_hint`/`defaults_hoist_audit_hint` (see `docs/lazuli_way/feature-defaults.md`).
- Reach for `query.sql` / `query.compose` for joins/aggregates, not a raw SQL string buried in a `@fn` Go handler. Raw SQL hidden behind an opaque `fn` trips `ESC-RAWSQL-IN-HANDLER-001`, which is non-waivable-to-silence — clear it by converting the read to a declared `query.sql`, not with a `# doctor:allow`.
- A `query.sql` must use one binding style with every param declared (`ESC-SQL-TENANCY-CONTRACT-001`) and either carry a tenant predicate or an `@actor.<privileged>` guard (`ESC-SCOPE-OVERRIDE-UNGUARDED-001`).
- Reach for a closed `state {}` bound to `transition`, not enum-by-command comments — declare the lifecycle's states as a named closed set (`lifecycle <field>` with `state … initial`/`terminal`) so every `transition.from`/`to` membership-checks against a typed lattice, instead of a `status:` field whose legal moves live in prose and are implied by which command ran (`LIFECYCLE-STATE-SET-UNDECLARED-001`; see `docs/lazuli_way/state-machines.md`).
- Reach for `restrict on_delete references <rel> via <fk>` on the protected resource, not a hand-copied `@fn` that runs a COUNT/EXISTS-then-reject referential guard. The generated `EXISTS` is tenant-scoped + soft-delete-aware by construction; a hand-written guard trips `SUGGEST-REFERENTIAL-GUARD-001` (see `docs/lazuli_way/referential-guards.md`).
- Reach for first-class `Money` (amount + currency + scale as one typed unit; the `_currency` column is enforced by codegen), not `@semantic.Money` string + a hand-added currency sibling, not a `_cents:Integer` + `_currency:Text` pair, not a bare `Decimal` whose currency lives in a comment. All three drift shapes trip `VOCAB-MONEY-SHAPE-001` (see `docs/lazuli_way/money.md`); currency code stays app data (no baked-in default).
- Reach for one feature = one capability: a feature's resources should relate (FK / `has_many` / `on_delete`). If they split into ≥2 unconnected clusters, you're bundling independent capabilities — split the feature (`LZI-FEATURE-COHESION-002`; see `docs/lazuli_way/one-feature-one-capability.md`).
- Suppress a doctor finding with the first-class node `@doctor.allow(<CODE>, reason: "why")` on the line ABOVE the construct (or at column 0 for file scope) — NOT a `#` comment. Always carry a reason; a bare `@doctor.allow(<CODE>)` (or the legacy comment) without one draws `DOCTOR-ALLOW-NO-REASON-001`, and the reason is REQUIRED when waiving an error-severity rule. The legacy `# doctor:allow <CODE> — reason "..."` comment still works but is deprecated (`DOCTOR-ALLOW-LEGACY-COMMENT-001`); run `lazuli fix --rule DOCTOR-ALLOW-LEGACY-COMMENT-001` to migrate it to the node.
- Do **NOT** write `#` comments in `.lzi`/`.lzx` — the design surface carries ZERO. Rationale → a `<feature>.ctx.md` context file; a construct's intent → its `purpose`/`doc`/`description` field; a waiver → `@doctor.allow(<CODE>, reason: "…")`. Section dividers, banners, gap notes, `TODO`/`NOTE` markers belong nowhere in the DSL — delete them. `LZI-COMMENT-PROSE-001` flags every `#` comment line (WARNING; ERROR under iron-hand; never blocks the gate); `lazuli fix --rule LZI-COMMENT-PROSE-001` clears the mechanical ones (empty `#`, dividers, legacy waivers) and reports the rest as manual relocations. See `docs/lazuli_way/comment-hygiene.md`.
- Before you write any `handlers/<x>.go`, scan the **runtime-surface index** — `docs/lazuli_way/runtime-surface.md` (intent-keyed: "hash a password → `auth.HashPassword`", "advance a state → declare a `transition`", "hex color → `@semantic.HexColor`"). The runtime owns the mechanism; you declare the resource. Reimplementing a runtime verb (hand-rolled argon2, a manual `UPDATE … status IN (…)` transition, a regex hex validator) trips `VOCAB-RUNTIME-REINVENTED-001`. See `docs/lazuli_way/delegate-to-runtime.md`.

See `docs/lazuli_way/escape-hatch-decision-tree.md` for the ordered "which surface do I reach for?" decision.

