## What's auto-wired vs. authored

The framework owns all the boilerplate for routing, registration, and policy
expansion. You should NOT be hand-writing any of this in `dist/go/`:

| Concern | Owner | Where it lives |
|---|---|---|
| `lazuli.Register(&cmd, &query, ...)` | codegen | `dist/go/<feature>/register.gen.go` (auto) |
| `cmd.Effect = lazuli.Returns(HandlerFn)` | codegen | inside `command.gen.go` `Effect:` field (auto from `handler @fn.X`) |
| `lazuli.Policy{Atoms: [...]}` expansion | codegen | inside `command.gen.go` / `query.gen.go` / `api.gen.go` (auto from `policies` block) |
| `ctx.now`, `ctx.user.org_id`, `actor.*` lookup | runtime | `readCtx` in `lazuli/handle.go` (auto resolves) |
| `@fn.<name>` binding fn lookup | runtime | `RegisterBindingFn` registry (you register, runtime resolves) |
| Migration FK ordering | codegen | `dist/go/migrations/<NNN>_<feature>_<resource>.sql` topo-sorted (auto) |

If you find yourself writing `<cmd>.Effect = lazuli.Returns(...)` or a
`patchPolicy()` shim in `dist/go/`, **stop** — that's a framework
workaround that should be filed as a WAR (workaround) ticket upstream.
Hand-written `dist/go/<feature>/register.go` (without `.gen.`) is the
escape hatch for things the framework doesn't yet auto-wire (today: only
`webhooks.Register(&contract, handler)`); the rest of register.gen.go
is fully generated.

## Do not

- Edit `dist/` directly — regen overwrites.
- Hand-write `<cmd>.Effect = lazuli.Returns(...)` or `<cmd>.Policy.Atoms = [...]` in `dist/go/` — file an upstream WAR instead.
- Add Go files outside `features/<x>/handlers/`, `features/<x>/domain/`, etc. — adapters belong in plugins.
- Commit with `lazuli doctor .` showing unsuppressed findings.
- Use `git commit --no-verify` to bypass pre-commit hooks (if any).
- Introduce `@plugin/{{app_name}}/<provider>` namespaces.
